## Privacy

By default, creating a container will make it <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`public`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Public`" pulumi-lang-go="`public`" pulumi-lang-python="`public`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`public`" pulumi-lang-java="`public`">`public`</span>, meaning that anybody knowing the endpoint can execute it.

A container can be made <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`private`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Private`" pulumi-lang-go="`private`" pulumi-lang-python="`private`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`private`" pulumi-lang-java="`private`">`private`</span> with the privacy parameter.

