Some record types can have multiple data with the same name (e.g., `A`, `AAAA`, `MX`, `NS`, etc.). You can duplicate a <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`scaleway.domain.Record`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`scaleway.domain.Record`" pulumi-lang-go="`domain.Record`" pulumi-lang-python="`domain.Record`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`scaleway.domain.Record`" pulumi-lang-java="`scaleway.domain.Record`">`scaleway.domain.Record`</span> resource with the same <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`name`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Name`" pulumi-lang-go="`name`" pulumi-lang-python="`name`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`name`" pulumi-lang-java="`name`">`name`</span>, and the records will be added.

Note however, that some records (e.g., CNAME, multiple dynamic records of different types) must be unique.

