### Simplify your rules using dynamic block and <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ForEach`" pulumi-lang-go="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-python="`for_each`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-java="`forEach`">`forEach`</span> loop

You can use <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ForEach`" pulumi-lang-go="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-python="`for_each`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-java="`forEach`">`forEach`</span> syntax to simplify the definition of your rules.
Let's suppose that your inbound default policy is to drop, but you want to build a list of exceptions to accept.
Create a local containing your exceptions (`locals.trusted`) and use the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ForEach`" pulumi-lang-go="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-python="`for_each`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`forEach`" pulumi-lang-java="`forEach`">`forEach`</span> syntax in a dynamic block:

